From: kuncy7 <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: account each peer's stats on its own

ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats() walks the per-peer entries of one wifili
stats message, but two things leak from one entry into the next:

- tx_dropped is set to 0 once before the loop and only ever added to,
  so every peer after the first gets the drops of all peers before it
  added to its tx_failed;
- a peer without nss_stats makes the function return, so the peers
  after it in the same message are not accounted at all.

Reset tx_dropped for every entry and skip only the entry that has no
stats.

Both found by Adriel Santos in his RD03v2 port
(github.com/ADCDS/openwrt-xiaomi-ax3000t-rd03v2, nss-peer-accounting).

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@ static void ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(st
 	struct ath11k_peer *peer;
 	struct nss_wifili_peer_ctrl_stats *pstats = NULL;
 	int i, j, i2;
-	u64 tx_packets, tx_bytes, tx_dropped = 0;
+	u64 tx_packets, tx_bytes, tx_dropped;
 	u64 rx_packets, rx_bytes, rx_dropped;
 
 	if (!ab->nss.stats_enabled)
@@ -152,6 +152,7 @@ static void ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(st
 
 	for (i = 0; i < stats->npeers; i++) {
 		pstats = &stats->wpcs[i];
+		tx_dropped = 0;
 
 		rcu_read_lock();
 		spin_lock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
@@ -173,7 +174,7 @@ static void ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(st
 		if (!peer->nss.nss_stats) {
 			spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 			rcu_read_unlock();
-			return;
+			continue;
 		}
 
 		if (pstats->tx.tx_success_cnt)
